{{!
    @template local_eventcalendar/access_rule

    A single access rule, inside a group (access_group).
    Rendered by the local_eventcalendar/access_rules module.

    Four regions filled by JavaScript according to the chosen type: rule type, subject (select or
    autocomplete), operator and value. The content of the last three depends on the previous choices,
    so it is not part of the template.

    The row items are bottom-aligned (align-items-end) because an autocomplete is taller than a select.

    The "message" region shows why a rule is invalid (item deleted from Moodle) or incomplete; in
    those cases the JavaScript also adds a red border to the row (border border-danger) and links the
    message to the row with aria-describedby. The row is a group for assistive technologies; its
    accessible name and the labels of the fields are set by the JavaScript.

    Example context (json):
    {
    }
}}
<div class="rounded p-2 mb-1" data-region="rule" role="group">
    <div class="d-flex flex-wrap align-items-end local-eventcalendar-gap-sm">
        <div data-region="type"></div>
        <div data-region="subject" class="local-eventcalendar-rulesubject"></div>
        <div data-region="comparison"></div>
        <div data-region="value"></div>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-link text-danger p-0 local-eventcalendar-push-end" data-action="remove-rule"
                title="{{#str}}accessremoverule, local_eventcalendar{{/str}}">
            {{#pix}}e/cancel, core, {{#str}}accessremoverule, local_eventcalendar{{/str}}{{/pix}}
        </button>
    </div>
    <div class="text-danger small mt-1" data-region="message"></div>
</div>
